# Referendums, by the rulebook ("Politics": the referendum, gaining votes, titled vampires, the
# Edge) and zero-vtes docs/rules-qa.md (1.1, 5.1, 5.3, 5.4, 5.8, 5.9, 46.2, 64.12).
# Sarah plays first; her prey is Alexis, her predator Pieter. Marek Hale is a prince (2 votes),
# Odile Fen a primogen (1 vote), Bastien Roe an archbishop (2 votes); Open Motion is a political
# action card.
seed 5
seat S sarah
seat X alexis
seat P pieter
crypt S "Marek Hale" *12
library S "Open Motion" *40
crypt X "Odile Fen" *12
library X "Open Motion" *40
crypt P "Bastien Roe" *12
library P "Iron Ward" *40
start

S> move S:uncontrolled:1 ready
S> move S:uncontrolled:1 ready
X> move X:uncontrolled:1 ready
X> move X:uncontrolled:1 ready
P> move P:uncontrolled:1 ready
S> next
S> next
expect turn 1 S minion

# A political action is undirected: the prey, then the predator, may block.
S> political S:ready:1 with S:hand:1
expect action political S blocks
X> pass
P> pass
expect action political S resolution

# The terms are chosen only once the action succeeds (rulebook, "The Political Action").
S> resolve success "Sarah gains 3 pool"
log public Marek Hale calls a referendum: “Sarah gains 3 pool”
expect action political S referendum

# The polling step opens with the cards played before votes are cast: the other Methuselahs
# first, from the caller's left, the caller last (64.12). Alexis and Pieter pass automatically.
expect window referendum minion
expect impulse S
reject S> vote for S:ready:1
S> pass
expect window polling minion
expect waiting S:vote

# Titled vampires: a prince has 2 votes (rulebook, "Titled Vampires"). Casting is a commitment:
# Sarah keeps the impulse and may cast another source (1.1).
S> vote for S:ready:1
log public Marek Hale casts 2 votes in favour
expect votes 2 0
expect impulse S
# The calling card is Sarah's 1 vote (5.4), and her one political action card vote: she can't
# burn another (46.2).
S> vote for card
expect votes 3 0
reject S> vote for S:hand:1
# A vampire's votes all go one way, and a cast can't be changed (1.1).
reject S> vote against S:ready:1 1
S> pass

# Alexis: her primogen (1 vote), then a political action card burned for 1 vote, replaced from
# her library. Only one card vote each (rulebook, "Political Action Cards").
expect impulse X
X> vote against X:ready:1
X> vote against X:hand:1
log public X burns Open Motion for 1 vote against
expect count X:hand 7
expect count X:ashHeap 1
expect votes 3 2
reject X> vote against X:hand:1
X> pass

# Pieter's archbishop: 2 votes.
P> vote against P:ready:1
expect votes 3 4
P> pass

# Every commitment gives everyone another chance before the tally (5.3): the polling closes only
# after a full round of passes with nothing cast.
expect impulse S
S> pass
expect impulse X
X> pass
# More votes against than for: it fails. The action itself succeeded, and the card is burned (5.8).
log public The referendum fails (3 for, 4 against)
log public The action succeeded
S> pass
expect action none
expect count S:ashHeap 1
expect pool S 30

# The Edge: burned for 1 vote (rulebook, "The Edge"). Abstaining passes the rest of the polling.
S> edge S
S> political S:ready:2 with S:hand:1
X> pass
P> pass
S> resolve success "Sarah gains 1 pool"
S> pass
S> vote for S:ready:2
S> pass
X> vote against X:ready:1
X> vote against X:hand:1
X> pass
P> abstain
log public P abstains from the rest of the referendum
# Alexis cast after Sarah passed, so Sarah may answer (5.3): 2 for, 2 against.
expect impulse S
expect votes 2 2
S> vote for edge
log public S burns the Edge for 1 vote in favour
expect edge none
expect votes 3 2
S> pass
X> pass
log public The referendum passes (3 for, 2 against)
S> pass
expect action none
# The caller applies what passed by hand.
S> pool +1
expect pool S 31

# Alexis's turn. A locked vampire still votes (rulebook, "Titled Vampires"): Sarah's princes
# acted last turn. A tie fails (rulebook, "The Referendum").
S> next
S> next
S> next
X> next
X> next
expect turn 2 X minion
X> political X:ready:1 with X:hand:1
P> pass
S> pass
X> resolve success
log public Odile Fen calls a referendum
X> pass
X> vote for X:ready:1
X> vote for card
X> pass
P> pass
expect card S:ready:1 locked true
S> vote against S:ready:1
S> pass
X> pass
P> pass
log public The referendum fails (2 for, 2 against)
X> pass
expect action none

# A political action whose vampire is no longer ready when it succeeds calls no referendum, and
# still ends successful (5.9).
X> political X:ready:2 with X:hand:1
P> pass
S> pass
X> move X:ready:2 torpor
X> resolve success
log public No referendum: Odile Fen is no longer ready
X> pass
expect action none
